      <title>Philly to put up 'No Stopping' signs along bike lanes citywide after receiving $1 million from PennDOT</title>
      <link>https://www.phillyvoice.com/philly-bike-lanes-no-stopping-signs-penndot-loading-zones/?utm_source=pv-rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=pv-site</link>
      <description>A $1 million grant from PennDOT will pay for Philadelphia to install 'No Stopping' signs along bike lanes citywide. The change is needed after a law banned temporary parking in bike lanes and increasing penalties for violators. The current signs only say 'No Parking.'</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.phillyvoice.com/philly-bike-lanes-no-stopping-signs-penndot-loading-zones/?utm_source=pv-rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=pv-site</guid>
